title: Anika
---
Player: hello, what's your thing?
Anika: I show off the built in palette that provides some common rich text tags.
Player: oh cool
Anika: It lets you do things like make words [b]bold[/b]
Anika: or maybe you want them [u]underlined[/u]
Anika: or even [i]italicised[/i].
Anika: or [b][i]wombo[u]combo[/i] them[/u] together[/b] even.
Player: that's awesome.
Anika: you can even define [custom]custom[/custom] markers for [fancy]fancy[/fancy] looks.
Anika: You can see these in the [link="https://yarnspinner.dev/docs/godot/gdscript/07-samples/13-replacement-markup/#anika-a-palette-and-a-style" external=true]demo tags markup palette[/link] inside the sample.

Player: Is that all?
Anika: nope, we also have support for styles.
Anika: If you have a defined [style=h2]style[/style] in a style marker processor we can pass it through to the text label.
Player: that is cool.
Anika: yeah I think so.
===
